  "question": {
    "text": "A shell is fired from a fixed artillery gun with an initial speed u such that it hits the target on the ground at a distance <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> from it. If <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> are the values of the time taken by it to hit the target in two possible ways, the product <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know for complementary angle range is same for same projection speed.<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> &hellip;.. (i)<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> &hellip;.. (ii)<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi>n&#952;c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfrac></math> .&hellip; (iii)<br />From equation (i) and (ii)<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br />(Using the value of R from equation iii)<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>"
  }
